  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phytosanitary scoping mission Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At the request of Bangladeshi government, this project set out to identify potential cooperation opportunities between Bangladesh and the Netherlands on strengthening the Bangladeshi electronic certification system and it&#x2019;s phytosanitary services, such as phytosanitary inspection, plant quarantine, and integrated pest risk analysis.Currently, being unable to comply with international phytosanitary standards and not making use of e-certification are some of the issues limiting Bangladesh to export to international markets. Besides that, not having the right phytosanitary systems in place is also for Dutch companies a challenge when doing business in Bangladesh.This project will map what obstacles and bottlenecks there are in the phytosanitary environment of Bangladesh and how they can be overcome. The resulting in-depth assessment will contribute to the formulation of follow-up projects initiating cooperation between Bangladesh and the Netherlands on capacity-building in the phytosanitary sector and electronic certification processes.</narrative>
  </description>
